From eb36606301965d4032033e5efe0fa4ff8f4e4ef8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Thu, 24 Oct 2026 08:05:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] rdna-boosts: block 15: q8_1 cache view-offset mis-hit fix + source range guard

q8_1: gate cache view-reuse on pointer equality + validate source range

The Q8_1 on-the-fly quantize cache is keyed by the ROOT tensor identity, but
the arena buffer is filled from the (possibly offset) VIEW pointer. An
offset view stored its rows under the root's identity, so a later op with
the same root + canonical row layout could hit an entry quantized from a
different base pointer -- and when the view's compute buffer was
reallocated (graph replay / compute-buffer pool reuse) the quantize kernel
read through a stale pointer: HSA_STATUS_ERROR_MEMORY_APERTURE_VIOLATION on
decode, silent stale reads on multi-GPU.

- The mmvq (x4) and unary (x2) src1_key walks now stop at the first pointer
  change, so offset-free views keep the shared root entry and offset views
  get their own cache entry (allocated from the existing arena).
- q8_1_src_range_ok() (common.cuh) checks the source read range against the
  root buffer's allocation before every quantize_row_q8_1_cuda and fused
  gated-q8_1 launch; a stale pointer now aborts loudly with the layout
  logged instead of faulting or reading reused memory.

Verified (Qwen3.8-27B Q6_K_XL, single V620 gfx1030): decode bench
pp512/tg128 clean (18.5 t/s), PPL 2.9968 default vs 2.9963 with
GGML_CUDA_Q8_1_CACHE_EXACT=1 (identical), test-backend-ops MUL_MAT 2/2
passed.
